= The ecological base

== Actual co-presence precedes coordinates

#object-entry(elements.receiver_configuration_calculus)

The first formula is not a state vector.  It is the incidence
$
  E arrow.r B_1 times dots.c times B_m.
$
The product addresses possible local receiver positions.  The object $E$
contains the positions which actually occur together, including plural
occurrences with the same addressed tuple.  Completing $E$ to the product
would assert combinations which the ecology never supplied.

This distinction controls the calculus.  A derivative with respect to
receiver $i$ is not created by writing a coordinate subscript.  It requires
an actual tangent in $E$ which varies that receiver while fixing the others.
When every admissible tangent changes several receivers together, only that
joint direction exists.

The same principle holds in a discrete ecology.  There, the tangent is
replaced by an admitted neighboring event or correspondence.  Adding an
unobserved one-coordinate successor would be the discrete equivalent of a
false infinitesimal.

== The accessible region is generated, not ambient

At one incidence $e$, the configuration fiber $X_e$ is received jointly:
$
  q_e:X_e arrow.r product_i Y_(i,e).
$
Typed comparisons generate a region:
$
  Omega_e
  =
  {x:b_a(e,q_e(x)) bowtie_a 0
  " for all active "a}.
$
The geometry is therefore relative in a precise sense.  The receiver, the
comparison, and the configuration participate in the definition of
$Omega_e$.  There is no need to place them inside an observer-independent
rendering box first.

Each equality $b_a=0$ is an oriented boundary sheet.  Intersections of these
sheets make corners and higher codimension faces.  Where their differentials
lose the expected rank, the existing local coordinate law no longer
continues regularly.  That discriminant is the exact candidate for a
FOUNDing or phase seam.  A visible kink may testify about such a seam, but it
does not define one.

== Basis, unit, and normalization

An axis is a typed local fiber; a unit is a nonzero local frame in it.
If $v=[v]_u u$ and the receiver chooses $u'=v$, then
$
  [v]_(u')=1.
$
This is why a nonzero length can always have coordinate $1$ in a receiver
normalized to that length.  The transformation $u arrow.r u'$ retains the
scale which the reported $1$ omits.

Normalization is consequently not an assertion that all lengths are equal.
It is a rebase in a local comparison.  Orthonormalization is the corresponding
construction for a nondegenerate inner-product frame; it owes that inner
product and can fail or change species in an indefinite or singular fiber.

== The Swing differentiates relation

For four ordered marks, the cross-ratio Swing is projectively invariant.
Its differential is
$
  frac(dif chi,chi)
  =
  frac(dif A-dif C,A-C)
  +frac(dif B-dif D,B-D)
  -frac(dif A-dif D,A-D)
  -frac(dif B-dif C,B-C).
$
Every term compares a difference of motions with a difference of positions.
Common projective recharting cancels.  The expression therefore detects the
relative change of the four-member configuration.

This gives the Swing a precise role in a dynamic ecology.  It is not a
universal update rule imposed on every system.  It is the projective
differential available whenever four ordered incidences furnish its marks.
Another application may supply a different invariant, but it enters the same
receiver-relative calculus.

== One relating, and the term that belongs to neither argument

#object-entry(elements.tower_cross_term_identity)

The Swing above differentiates a relation of four marks; this identity reads the
relating of *two* and names what the pair returns that neither member carries.
The cross term is that object.  It is absent exactly at the square corner, which
is why a right angle carries no relating and why an orthogonal decomposition is
the case where the parts say nothing about each other.

Two readings usually kept apart are the same algebra.  A triangle of contacts
returns the Law of Cosines; a superposition of two oriented contributions returns
an interference sum; and the substitution $alpha_1=a$, $alpha_2=-b e^(i gamma)$
carries one to the other term by term.  Whatever an ecology's returns are made
of, if two of them meet at one consequence then the meeting contributes a term
depending on their relative turn, and that term is the whole content of the
meeting.

= The notation, and what it is for

Notation here is an instrument for reasoning, not a decoration on results
already obtained.  Each of the four below is adopted because it makes a
distinction *visible in the symbol* that the framework insists on and the
conventional spelling hides.

== A bra is a receiver; a ket is a construction

#object-entry(elements.bra_receiver_ket_construction)

Writing $chevron.l psi,phi chevron.r$ computes the same number and presents the
two arguments as one species.  They are not: one is what is presented and the
other is what presents it.  Riesz makes the conflation harmless for the *value*
and lossy for the *reading*, and the reading is what the framework is about.
The payoff is immediate: a receiver family orthonormal in a declared metric is
complete exactly when it resolves the identity, so non-reconstruction is no
longer a caveat carried in prose -- it is the inequality
$sum_i ketbra(a_i, a_i) != I$, and the defect $I-P$ is a computable object.
The metric is not decoration: for a family that merely spans, the sum is the
frame operator rather than a projection, and reconstruction runs through the
dual frame.

== Crossing depth, and why the correction terms alternate

#object-entry(elements.crossing_depth_inversion)

An arrangement of $n$ regions cuts its ambient face into $2^n$ pieces, one per
membership word: the fork is *per curve* and a region is a word, not a set.
Grading by how many regions contain a piece recovers inclusion--exclusion, whose
alternating sign is the Möbius function of the Boolean lattice -- which is to
say that the correction series is an *inverted* one.  Depth one is what the
parts carry alone; every deeper term is what a meeting carries and no part does.
That is the tower's cross term at arity $k$, and it is why the pieces of depth
at least two are the constrained ones.

== Flux locality is the parallelization license

#object-entry(elements.divergence_locality_parallelization)

This is the part of the notation that has to survive contact with an apparatus.
The divergence theorem says an interior speaks only through its boundary, so a
partition decouples exactly to the extent that its terms are boundary fluxes --
and every term that is not a flux is a barrier.  Interior elimination is
independent per subdomain and the interface is the only meeting; that is domain
decomposition, and it is the statement as an algorithm.

The instructive case is the one that *fails* to decouple.  Incompressibility is
a statement about the domain and not about any cell, so the pressure it
determines is an elliptic solve with globally supported Green's function.
Advection and diffusion parallelize; the projection does not.  A body whose
local moves are cheap and whose *join* is global has the same shape, and the
join is where the barrier will be.

The caution belongs in the same breath: this licenses a decomposition and never
a schedule.  Whether co-present events may be enacted in any order is a property
of the material, to be proved for that material, and no theorem about coupling
supplies it.

== A diagram's value is a word

#object-entry(elements.diagram_word_resummation)

Chen's theorem is a completeness statement about a face: iterated integrals are
*exactly* the homotopy functionals on path space, so that face sees ordered
transport up to homotopy and nothing further, and endpoint evaluation is the
strictly coarser face the winding separates from it.  Their algebra is the
shuffle algebra on words, which is why the evaluated tetrahedral vacuum diagram
reduces to four-letter words in a seven-letter alphabet.  Ordered transport and
word combinatorics are one algebra.

Replacing an infinite family of such words by a closed return is condensation,
and the cited Fermi-gas result is evidence that it is achievable outside a
perturbative regime -- with the physical gas serving as a second apparatus chart
for one law.  It is an instance and not a method, and the boundary field says so.

= The limit is indexed by its receiver

The integral in the next part presupposes a convergence, and until this part
that convergence was borrowed silently from the ambient analysis.  Borrowing it
is lawful; borrowing it *without an index* is the absolute frame returning by
the back door.  The convergence taxonomy already separates the species; what it
did not carry is a relation that says *at which receiver* a net has settled.

== A limit is the exhaustion of one receiver's distinguishing tests

#object-entry(elements.receiver_indexed_convergence)

Nothing new is proved about any classical limit and nothing classical is
displaced.  Inside one index this is exactly convergence in $Y_rho$, with every
ordinary theorem intact.  What the index buys is that two receivers may now
disagree *as a theorem with a witness* rather than as a paradox, and that the
phrase "the limit" is no longer permitted to name an unstated frame.

The reading in the transport vocabulary is the one that matters for the machine:
a net has converged at $rho$ when continued transport can no longer contribute a
difference $rho$ is able to experience.  Convergence is not arrival at a point.
It is the *exhaustion of a declared family of differences*, and the point is
whatever remains once that family is spent.

== Epsilon and delta live in two different grains

#object-entry(elements.modulus_of_transport)

The classical statement writes one absolute-value bar on both sides of the
implication and thereby identifies the two grains without saying so.  Separating
them exposes the object the alternation was always asserting: a map $omega_a$
running *backwards* along $f$, from what the observer demands to what the source
must supply.  Continuity is the existence of that transport; the familiar
hierarchy -- pointwise, uniform, Lipschitz, Hölder -- is a hierarchy on $omega_a$
and on nothing else.

== Disagreement between receivers is an obstruction, not an inconsistency

#object-entry(elements.limit_receiver_noncommutation)

The staircase is worth stating plainly because it is the cleanest available
demonstration that a limit is not a property of a sequence.  The same sequence
converges and does not converge, exactly, at two receivers of the same object.
Arc length does not factor continuously through the image, and the sequence is
the certificate.  This is receiver non-reconstruction at the level of limits:
agreement of one face does not transport to a face that face does not determine.

Golab's theorem then supplies the *hand* of the failure.  Length can only be
lost in the limit, never gained, so the obstruction is oriented.  An obstruction
with a hand is a stronger return than an obstruction without one, and the
difference is exactly the difference between OPEN and a signed residual.

== "Undefined" names an empty equalizer under a declared target

#object-entry(elements.one_sided_face_equalizer)

The side of an approach is part of the receiver, not part of the expression.
Once that is said, $1\/x$ at the origin stops being an exception: three declared
targets return three exact values, and the classical verdict "undefined" is the
third receiver's OPEN under one of them.  On the one-point compactification --
where the expression is the chart inversion $[z:w] |-> [w:z]$ and $infinity$ has
no sides -- the equalizer closes and there is nothing left to reconcile.

This is the general shape and not a trick played on one example.  A construction
that reports "undefined" without naming its target has reported the emptiness of
an equalizer it did not declare.

= One calculus for flow and event

== Smooth continuation and discrete wall crossing

#object-entry(elements.receiver_stratified_fundamental_theorem)

The theorem decomposes exact change into two terms:
$
  "change"
  =
  "transported chamber flow"
  +
  "transported seam jumps".
$
Neither term is privileged.  A smooth deformation contributes through a
covariant derivative.  A quantized boundary event contributes through an
exact difference.  A mixed ecology carries both.

The formula also clarifies measurement over orders of time.  The endpoint
difference is not attributed to one instantaneous state.  It is factored
through the entire oriented path, including each chamber current and each
seam.  When a lower constituent no longer appears in the transported
successor, it may depart; the equality retains its consequence rather than a
perfect copy of its former interior.

== Lambda as evaluation of a supplied ecology

Package the local data as
$
  cal(K)
  =
  (E,pi_X,q,b,nabla,J,nu).
$
Here $E$ is actual co-presence, $q$ the joint receiver, $b$ the boundary
family, $nabla$ chamber transport, $J$ seam conduct, and $nu$ an optional
decoration such as prime valuation.  For a path $gamma$, define
$
  Lambda_cal(K)(gamma,S_0)
  =
  cal(P)_(0 arrow.r 1) S_0
  +
  integral_0^1 cal(P)_(t arrow.r 1) nabla_(dot(gamma)) S_t dif t
  +
  sum_k cal(P)_(t_k^+ arrow.r 1) Delta_k S.
$
By the stratified fundamental theorem this is $S_1$.

This is the disciplined sense in which the calculus is universal.  Lambda is
not a content-free law which guesses the ecology.  It evaluates the exact
incidence, boundary, transport, and seam data the ecology supplies.  The same
construction can receive arithmetic, geometry, a physical simulation, an
algorithm, language, or a biological network without asserting that those
domains share one vocabulary or one domain equation.

= Second-order ecology

== Co-presence is not curvature

#object-entry(elements.receiver_relative_second_order_calculus)

For a two-direction square, the mixed finite difference
$
  H_(i j) S=S_(11)-S_(10)-S_(01)+S_(00)
$
is the part not attributable to either direction alone.  It is an exact
incidence term.  If $S_(a b)=a b$, then $H_(i j) S=1$: the joint feature exists
only when both inputs are present.

Curvature asks another question.  Transport first along $i$ and then $j$;
transport first along $j$ and then $i$; compare the two returns.  Their
difference is the ordered residual
$
  cal(R)_(i j)
  =
  U_(10,11) U_(00,10)
  -
  U_(01,11) U_(00,01).
$
The two paths may agree while the mixed incidence remains nonzero.  This is
why $partial^2=0$, a commuting diagram, or a vanishing curvature does not mean
that second-order interaction disappeared.

== Receiver--prime mixed curvature

Let $Delta_p$ admit or resolve a prime-place boundary and let $V_i$ be an
admissible receiver direction.  Then
$
  cal(C)_(i,p)
  =
  nabla_(V_i) Delta_p-Delta_p nabla_(V_i)
$
asks whether those operations commute.

- If $cal(C)_(i,p)=0$, the prime cut transports naturally through that
  receiver motion.
- If it is nonzero, the receiver change alters which arithmetic face the cut
  exposes, or the arithmetic cut alters the receiver's continuation.
- Even when it vanishes, the symmetric mixed difference can record
  co-present receiver--prime incidence.

This is the higher-order vector calculus requested by the laboratory.  Its
directions are not axes of an absolute ambient space.  They are admitted
motions and discrete differences in the actual incidence ecology.

= The arithmetic field

== Valuation fibers retain composition

#object-entry(elements.graded_arithmetic_accessibility_current)

The current
$
  frak(A)_e(bold(X))
  =
  sum_alpha [C_(alpha,e)] bold(X)^alpha
$
retains what a scalar “number of accessible primes” cannot.  Each coefficient
is the oriented population occupying one valuation address.  Its degree-one
part contains primitive prime axes.  Its degree-two part distinguishes
$
  X_p^2
  quad "from" quad
  X_p X_q.
$
The first is repeated traversal of one prime axis; the second is a crossing
of two distinct prime axes.

The formal variables do not claim that primes are spatial coordinate axes.
They address exact multiplicative directions supplied by unique
factorization.  A geometric receiver may later embed those addresses into a
simplicial complex, logarithmic chart, circle, conic, or another surface.
That embedding is a face of the valuation current and owes its own transport
law.

== Probability is a later receiver

Applying an augmentation $epsilon$ gives
$
  Z_e(bold(X))=epsilon(frak(A)_e(bold(X))).
$
One may then normalize a declared finite measure and form conditional
recurrence ratios.  That probability face is exact in its event algebra, but
it is downstream of the occurrence current.  It does not turn the
deterministic wall crossings into ontological chance.

Likewise, loss is an oriented residual between two transported currents.  Its
sign refers to the chosen comparison orientation.  It is not reward,
punishment, or a scalar property attached to one arithmetic object.

== Prime admission is a boundary operation

#object-entry(elements.prime_cut_incidence_calculus)

A new place $p$ cuts out the occurrences divisible by $p$.  The first
difference is negative because those occurrences cross out of the survivor
region.  Admitting distinct $p$ and $q$ in either order gives the same static
sieve population, so the cut commutator vanishes.  Their mixed second
difference is nevertheless the complete population divisible by $p q$.

This is a concrete arithmetic instance of the second-order distinction:
$
  "zero cut curvature"
  quad != quad
  "zero joint incidence".
$
Prime squares require the valuation layer $v_p=2$; applying the same
idempotent admission twice would erase that distinction.

= The interval 113 to 127

#object-entry(elements.prime_interval_wall_current)

The familiar refinement table is now a single path in configuration space:

